Brand Impersonation Phishing – Duolingo

Severity: Medium
Status: Confirmed Phishing – No Compromise
Category: Social Engineering / Brand Impersonation

1. Executive Summary

On July 13, 2025, the mailbox inquiry@mydfir.com received a phishing email impersonating Duolingo. The message originated from a free Italian email provider (libero.it) and was sent via authenticated SMTP infrastructure.

Although the email contained no malicious links or attachments, analysis determined it was an initial-stage social engineering attempt designed to establish rapport and potentially deliver malicious content in a follow-up message.

2. Incident Overview

Display-name spoof: “Duolingo”

Sender address: duolingo.ads@libero.it

Authenticated submission via Libero Mail SMTP (ESMTPSA)

Attacker connection from French residential IP: 90.160.50.35

No embedded links or attachments

No user interaction observed

This activity aligns with early-stage phishing reconnaissance and brand impersonation tactics.

3. Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)

Sender Email: duolingo.ads@libero.it

Source IP: 90.160.50.35 (Orange S.A., France)

Claimed Hostname: 5.9.230.8 (Hetzner, Germany – likely spoofed)

Additional Infrastructure Observed: 213.209.10.34

Mail Server Processing: srv7.swhc.ca

4. Investigation Timeline

Date/Time Received:
July 13, 2025 – 11:50:03 EDT (UTC-4)

Observations:

Email passed SPF, DKIM, and DMARC for libero.it

Authentication success due to legitimate SMTP account usage

No malicious payload delivered in initial message

No additional follow-up emails detected

No evidence of compromise or lateral movement.

5. Technical Analysis

The attacker authenticated to Libero Mail using valid credentials (ESMTPSA).

The message passed domain-level authentication checks because it was legitimately sent from libero.it.

Brand impersonation occurred via display-name spoofing (“Duolingo”).

Messaging style matched influencer outreach/social collaboration pretexts.

This indicates a staged phishing approach rather than mass spam delivery.

